<h2>Beginner — 9 Habits That Save Context</h2>

<p>The first step to using Claude Code well isn't a fancy feature — it's <strong>the habit of conserving context</strong>. Context is the total amount of conversation and code the model can hold at once, and when it fills up, Claude starts forgetting things you already agreed on and saying odd stuff. If you've ever thought "I literally just told you this," context was probably the culprit. This document covers the beginner nine of this Tip series' 28, and every tip links to the official docs so you can dig deeper whenever you like.</p>

